From: Che-Wei Chuang <cnoize@andestech.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jan 2025 11:26:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/53] swdtb: uart: update current-speed property based on
 CONFIG_BAUDRATE (#136)

Update the UART nodes in the device tree to reflect the value of CONFIG_BAUDRATE.
If the current-speed property already exists, its value is updated to match CONFIG_BAUDRATE.
If the property does not exist, it is added with the correct value.

This current-speed property will be passed to OpenSBI to configure the baud rate
when it displays messages, ensuring accurate UART communication during system initialization.

Signed-off-by: Che-Wei Chuang <cnoize@andestech.com>

Reviewed-on: https://gitea.andestech.com/RD-SW/u-boot.official/pulls/136
Reviewed-by: randolph <randolph@andestech.com>
